            <ArticleTitle>[Mycotic aneurysm of the coronary artery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>771-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mycotic aneurysm of the coronary artery occurs in less than 1% of patients with infective endocarditis and only few cases of successful treatment has been described in the literature. The paper presents a case of 64 years old man with infective endocarditis of the mitral valve, complicated with a development of mycotic aneurysm of the right coronary artery, who was successfully surgically treated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
